      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the given system of equations, we will use the method of elimination. The given system is:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3x - 5y &= -11, \\quad \\text{(1)} \\\\\n7x + 2y &= -12. \\quad \\text{(2)}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nWe will eliminate one of the variables by making the coefficients of \\(y\\) in both equations equal in magnitude but opposite in sign. To do this, we will multiply equation (1) by 2 and equation (2) by 5:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n2(3x - 5y) &= 2(-11), \\\\\n5(7x + 2y) &= 5(-12).\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n6x - 10y &= -22, \\quad \\text{(3)} \\\\\n35x + 10y &= -60. \\quad \\text{(4)}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nNext, we add equations (3) and (4) to eliminate \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\n(6x - 10y) + (35x + 10y) = -22 + (-60).\n\\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[\n6x + 35x - 10y + 10y = -82,\n\\]\n\nwhich reduces to:\n\n\\[\n41x = -82.\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(x\\), we get:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-82}{41} = -2.\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(x = -2\\), we substitute this value back into equation (1) to solve for \\(y\\):\n\n\\[\n3(-2) - 5y = -11.\n\\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[\n-6 - 5y = -11.\n\\]\n\nAdding 6 to both sides, we get:\n\n\\[\n-5y = -5.\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(y\\), we get:\n\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-5}{-5} = 1.\n\\]\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(-2, 1)}.\n\\]",
